ARWINI put the worst case at up to 75,000 records and HAZ and NDR estimated more than 70,000; neither speaks of 70,000 patient records with health and billing data, and the KVN says the patient data it supplies are anonymised. The Lower Saxony data protection commissioner received a breach notification and is checking whether it was timely; no source mentions a BSI notification, KRITIS obligations or NIS2 status, and the police, not Kairos's claim alone, confirm the data outflow and the Kairos attribution.
